<title>TURKEY: Turk Netas Q1 profits rise 58.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Netas Q1 profits rise 58.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 1,271.80 vs     803.35</p>
<p>    Net profit		  1,586.44 vs   1,002.10</p>
<p>    Net sales		   6,663.36 vs   2,758.48</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  2,003.01 vs     930.50</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  813.94 vs     747.09</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 261.81 vs     113.91</p>
<p>    Interest paid		  58.08 vs	 6.65</p>
<p>    Total debts		 8,671.61 vs   5,305.89</p>
<p>    Equity		     10,897.94 vs   5,609.65</p>
<p>    Capital		     1,247.40 vs   1,247.40</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish telecommunications equipment producer Netas-Northern Electric Telekominikasyon A.S. is owned 51.85 percent by Canada's Northern Telecom Int..</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
